00:04:57,272 --> 00:05:03,272
Some things were never meant to be controlled.

2
00:09:54,545 --> 00:10:00,545
Geostorm is a action, science fiction, thriller film directed by Dean Devlin.

3
00:14:51,818 --> 00:14:57,818
After an unprecedented series of natural disasters threatened the planet, the world's leaders came together to
create an intricate network of satellites to control the global climate and keep everyone safe.

4
00:19:49,090 --> 00:19:55,090
But now, something has gone wrong: the system built to protect Earth is attacking it, and it becomes a race against the
clock to uncover the real threat before a worldwide geostorm wipes out everything and everyone along with it.

5
00:24:46,363 --> 00:24:52,363
Jake Lawson, played by Gerard Butler.

6
00:29:43,636 --> 00:29:49,636
Ute Fassbinder, played by Alexandra Maria Lara.

7
00:34:40,909 --> 00:34:46,909
Max Lawson, played by Jim Sturgess.

8
00:39:38,181 --> 00:39:44,181
U.S. Secret Service Agent Sarah Wilson, played by Abbie Cornish.

9
00:44:35,454 --> 00:44:41,454
U.S. Secretary of State Leonard Dekkom, played by Ed Harris.

10
00:49:32,727 --> 00:49:38,727
U.S. President Andrew Palma, played by Andy Garcia.

11
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Geostorm is a 2017 American science-fiction disaster film directed, cowritten,
and coproduced by Dean Devlin (in his feature directorial debut).

12
00:59:27,272 --> 00:59:33,272
The film stars Gerard Butler, Jim Sturgess, Abbie
Cornish, Ed Harris, and Andy García.

13
01:04:24,545 --> 01:04:30,545
It follows a satellite designer who tries to save the world from a storm of epic
proportions caused by malfunctioning climate-controlling satellites.

14
01:09:21,818 --> 01:09:27,818
Principal photography began on October 20, 2014, in New Orleans, Louisiana.

15
01:14:19,090 --> 01:14:25,090
After poor test screenings, reshoots took place in December 2016 under executive producer
Jerry Bruckheimer, writer Laeta Kalogridis, and new director Danny Cannon.

16
01:19:16,363 --> 01:19:22,363
To date, the film is the only co-production
between Skydance Media and Warner Bros.

17
01:24:13,636 --> 01:24:19,636
Geostorm was released in the United States on October 20, 2017, in all formats, and heavily underperformed at the box
office, grossing only $221.6 million worldwide against a $120–130 million budget, losing Warner Bros.

18
01:29:10,909 --> 01:29:16,909
$71.6 million.

19
01:34:08,181 --> 01:34:14,181
The film was also widely panned by critics for its muddled storytelling,
underdeveloped characters and lackluster visual effects.

20
01:39:05,454 --> 01:39:11,454
The film explores themes of future, artificial intelligence
(a.i.), weather manipulation, end of the world, murder.

21
01:44:02,727 --> 01:44:08,727
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
